From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:02:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?test(goldens):=20each=20writer=20on=20its=20own?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20one=20generated=20document,=20a=20writer@<agent>?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20snapshot=20per=20writer?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The goldens measure losses end to end, so a loss could be the source reader's
or the target writer's. A generated view that fills every field the
conversation view carries is derived once and projected for each of the seven
agents alone, read back by that agent's adapter and compared. Every writer
keeps the text; cursor drops one of three tool calls; no writer keeps a
delegation's own turns. The qualifier concern on round_trip is re-anchored
(--supersedes) after the function moved. Record: pr/26.
